### Before the run
- [ ] Network adapter set to host-only/custom VMnet (not NAT/Bridged)
- [ ] Copy/paste, drag-and-drop, and shared folders disabled
- [ ] Guest reverted to clean, hardened snapshot
- [ ] tcpdump running on CAPE VM, writing to a run-specific file
- [ ] Fixed run duration confirmed (45 minutes)
- [ ] VirusTotal has confirmed anti-VM capability (if sample is tagged VM-aware)
- [ ] Sample SHA-256 verified against MalwareBazaar record

### During the run
- [ ] Sample submitted via CAPE
- [ ] In-guest Procmon, Regshot (pre-shot taken), Autoruns, FakeNet-NG
      all confirmed running (process + log file check)
- [ ] Start time noted

### After the run
- [ ] Capture stopped at fixed duration
- [ ] Regshot post-shot taken, Autoruns snapshot exported
- [ ] Procmon exported to CSV
- [ ] tcpdump stopped, pcap saved
- [ ] Completion state classified (completed / exited early / crashed / dormant)
- [ ] CAPE's own report pulled as secondary cross-check
- [ ] Results recorded in comparison table
- [ ] Guest reverted to clean snapshot again
